## Import

The RSC cloud cluster ID (UUID) is used to import the cluster. The values used when the cluster was created, such as the
region, the number of nodes, the instance type, the VPC, subnet and security groups and the S3 bucket, are read from
the configuration RSC recorded when it created the cluster. A configuration which doesn't match the imported cluster
plans a replacement of the cluster, so check the plan before applying it.

The values RSC doesn't record are taken from the configuration by the first apply after the import, without changing
or replacing the cluster: `cdm_version`, which may differ from the installed version if the cluster has been upgraded,
`force_cluster_delete_on_destroy`, the write-only `admin_email` and `admin_password`, and `vm_type` when the cluster was
created with the `STANDARD` VM type. The same applies to every create-time value of a cluster RSC has no create record
for, e.g. a cluster which wasn't created by RSC; the import then reports a warning and the provider trusts the
configuration to match the cluster.

